---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";

const pdfUrl = "https://aile3.ijs.si/dunja/SiKDD2025/Papers/IS2024_-_SIKDD_2025_paper_6.pdf";
const doiUrl = "https://doi.org/10.70314/ix.2025.sikdd.6";
const repoUrl = "https://github.com/daiapavlova02/defi_trends_semantic";

const metrics = [
	{ label: "AUC", baseline: "0.598", graph: "0.787", improvement: "+31.6%" },
	{ label: "F1-score", baseline: "0.384", graph: "0.480", improvement: "+25.0%" },
	{ label: "Precision", baseline: "0.341", graph: "0.490", improvement: "+43.7%" },
	{ label: "Recall", baseline: "0.440", graph: "0.470", improvement: "+6.8%" },
];

const graphFeatures = [
	{
		name: "Multi-chain count",
		description:
			"Number of distinct blockchains a protocol is deployed on — a proxy for user base and attack surface.",
	},
	{
		name: "Fork lineage",
		description:
			"Whether a protocol is forked from another, and how many forks derive from it — capturing inherited code and vulnerabilities.",
	},
	{
		name: "Past incident count",
		description:
			"Total prior security incidents involving the protocol, signalling underlying weaknesses or target value.",
	},
];

const references = [
	{
		text: "Chainalysis Team. 2023. “2022 Biggest Year Ever For Crypto Hacking with $3.8 Billion Stolen.” Chainalysis Blog.",
		url: "https://www.chainalysis.com/blog/2022-biggest-year-ever-for-crypto-hacking/",
	},
	{
		text: "G. Ke et al. 2017. “LightGBM: A Highly Efficient Gradient Boosting Decision Tree.” NeurIPS 30.",
	},
	{
		text: "J. Michel and P. Parrend. 2023. “Graph-Based Intelligent Cyber Threat Detection System.” CRC Press.",
	},
	{
		text: "D. Pavlova. 2025. “DeFi Security Trends: Semantic Knowledge Graph Analysis.” Code & dataset.",
		url: "https://github.com/daiapavlova02/defi_trends_semantic",
	},
	{
		text: "L. Sadlek et al. 2025. “Severity-Based Triage of Cybersecurity Incidents Using Kill Chain Attack Graphs.” JISA 89.",
	},
	{
		text: "S. Werner et al. 2021. “SoK: Decentralized Finance (DeFi).” arXiv:2101.08778.",
		url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.08778",
	},
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Research — Daria Pavlova"
	description="Graph-based feature engineering for DeFi security incident severity prediction — published research by Daria Pavlova."
>
	<Header current="research" />
	<main id="main-content" class="interior-page page-frame">
		<header class="interior-intro interior-intro--wide research-intro">
			<p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Research · Publication</p>
			<h1 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
				Graph-based feature engineering for DeFi security incident severity prediction
			</h1>
		</header>

		<div class="research-meta" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
			<div class="research-meta--authors">
				<p class="mono-label">Authors</p>
				<p>
					Daria Pavlova<br />
					Inna Novalija<br />
					Dunja Mladenić
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="research-meta--venue">
				<p class="mono-label">Venue</p>
				<p>
					Information Society 2025, SiKDD<br />
					6–10 October 2025<br />
					Ljubljana, Slovenia
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="research-meta--links">
				<p class="mono-label">Access</p>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={pdfUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Paper (PDF) ↗</a></li>
					<li><a href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Code &amp; dataset ↗</a></li>
					<li><a href={doiUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DOI ↗</a></li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="research-section" aria-labelledby="abstract-title">
			<p class="mono-label" id="abstract-title">Abstract</p>
			<div class="research-section-body">
				<p class="research-lede">
					Which DeFi security incidents will escalate into severe financial losses? We integrate a
					semantic knowledge graph of the DeFi ecosystem — protocol fork lineage, multi-chain
					deployments and historical incidents — into a gradient boosting classifier. Graph-based
					features lift predictive performance substantially over an incident-only baseline, with a
					particularly large gain in precision and a significantly reduced false alarm rate.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="research-stats" aria-label="Key results" data-animate>
			<div class="research-stat">
				<p class="mono-label">AUC</p>
				<p class="research-stat-value research-stat-value--accent">0.787</p>
				<p class="research-stat-note">vs. 0.598 baseline — a 31.6% relative improvement</p>
			</div>
			<div class="research-stat">
				<p class="mono-label">Precision</p>
				<p class="research-stat-value research-stat-value--accent">0.490</p>
				<p class="research-stat-note">+43.7% over baseline — far fewer false alarms</p>
			</div>
			<div class="research-stat">
				<p class="mono-label">Incidents</p>
				<p class="research-stat-value research-stat-value--data" data-count="1608">1,608</p>
				<p class="research-stat-note">DeFi security incidents, 2020–2025, publicly reported</p>
			</div>
			<div class="research-stat">
				<p class="mono-label">Severe losses</p>
				<p class="research-stat-value research-stat-value--data" data-count="402">402</p>
				<p class="research-stat-note">incidents above the $2.21M severity threshold</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="research-section" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
			<p class="mono-label" id="approach-title">Approach</p>
			<div class="research-section-body">
				<p>
					A semi-automated pipeline combines the Rekt database, the DeFiLlama API and SlowMist Hacked
					into a Neo4j knowledge graph. Protocol, incident and blockchain nodes are connected by
					<span class="feature-name">fork-of</span>, <span class="feature-name">deployed-on</span> and
					<span class="feature-name">incident-involves</span> relations. From this graph we derive
					structural features for each incident, computed strictly before the incident occurs:
				</p>
				<ul class="feature-list">
					{graphFeatures.map((feature) => (
						<li>
							<span class="feature-name">{feature.name}</span>
							<span>{feature.description}</span>
						</li>
					))}
				</ul>
				<p style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">
					These graph features are combined with temporal and categorical incident features in a
					LightGBM classifier. A severe incident is one exceeding the 75th percentile of losses —
					$2.21M — yielding 402 severe cases out of 1,608.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="research-section" aria-labelledby="results-title">
			<p class="mono-label" id="results-title">Results</p>
			<div class="research-section-body">
				<div class="research-table-wrap">
					<table class="research-table">
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th scope="col">Metric</th>
								<th scope="col">Baseline</th>
								<th scope="col">Semantic graph</th>
								<th scope="col">Improvement</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							{metrics.map((metric) => (
								<tr>
									<td class="metric-name">{metric.label}</td>
									<td>{metric.baseline}</td>
									<td>{metric.graph}</td>
									<td class="improvement">{metric.improvement}</td>
								</tr>
							))}
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
				<ul class="result-bars" aria-label="Baseline versus semantic graph model" data-animate>
					{metrics.map((metric, index) => (
						<li>
							<span class="metric-name">{metric.label}</span>
							<span class="bar-pair">
								<span class="bar bar--baseline">
									<span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style={`--w: ${Number(metric.baseline) * 100}%; --i-delay: ${index * 90}ms`}></span></span>
									<span class="bar-value">{metric.baseline}</span>
								</span>
								<span class="bar bar--graph">
									<span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style={`--w: ${Number(metric.graph) * 100}%; --i-delay: ${index * 90 + 150}ms`}></span></span>
									<span class="bar-value">{metric.graph}</span>
								</span>
							</span>
						</li>
					))}
				</ul>
				<p class="bar-legend" aria-hidden="true"><span>Baseline</span><span>Semantic graph</span></p>
				<p style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">
					Cross-validation confirms stability: the graph-augmented model averages AUC 0.809
					(std 0.027) across 5 folds, against 0.629 (std 0.036) for the baseline — a stronger and
					more consistent signal.
				</p>
			</div>
			<aside class="research-section-aside">
				<p class="mono-label" style="color: var(--muted);">Reading</p>
				<p style="font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0.55rem 0 0;">
					Graph features are only weakly correlated with each other — they contribute complementary
					signals rather than duplicating information.
				</p>
			</aside>
		</section>

		<section class="research-section" aria-labelledby="discussion-title">
			<p class="mono-label" id="discussion-title">Discussion</p>
			<div class="research-section-body">
				<p>
					Where an incident occurs in the ecosystem is as important as what it is. Incidents
					affecting widely forked or multi-chain protocols are more likely to cause severe losses,
					reflecting practical amplification effects through ecosystem dependencies.
				</p>
				<p>
					Graph-based risk factors can support auditors and insurers in identifying critical hot
					spots and pricing coverage more accurately than historical losses alone. Limitations
					remain: the dataset covers only publicly reported incidents, features are static and
					hand-engineered, and absolute performance leaves room before real-world deployment.
					Future work points toward dynamic graphs and graph neural networks.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="research-section research-references" aria-labelledby="references-title">
			<p class="mono-label" id="references-title">References</p>
			<div class="research-section-body">
				<ol>
					{references.map((reference) => (
						<li>
							{reference.url ? (
								<a href={reference.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{reference.text}</a>
							) : (
								reference.text
							)}
						</li>
					))}
				</ol>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="research-links" aria-label="Paper links">
			<a class="arrow-link" href={pdfUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
				<span>Read the paper</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
			</a>
			<a class="arrow-link" href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
				<span>Code &amp; dataset</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
			</a>
		</section>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</BaseLayout>
